<title>POLAND: POLISH LOCAL RADIOS SET UP ADVERTISING NETWORK.</title>
<headline>POLISH LOCAL RADIOS SET UP ADVERTISING NETWORK.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve Polish local radio stations set up on September 25 an advertising network, called &quot;Super FM&quot;, to jointly sell advertising time in all of the stations, a radio from the group said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The private Warsaw-based radio &quot;Eska&quot; said in a statement the advertisments would be broadcasted in all the 12 stations simultaneously.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
